# *Three Degrees of Freedom*

@left

![Slide image 20](assets/lect14e-hardy_weinberg_chi_square/warning-beacon.drawn.svg)

@right

- Six classes of data
  - two allele frequencies came from the data (total alleles minus one)
  - The sum of the predicted numbers is fixed by the sample size
- [This chi-square has 6 &#8211; 2 &#8211; 1 = 3 degrees of freedom]{color=red}
- Or once you have three values (total population, p1 and p2), you can calculate all of the other values.

